<question type="description"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Section 7: The Story — Part 8</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<h3>Section 7: The Story — Part 8</h3>
<p><strong>The Threat</strong></p>
<p><em>Narrative note: The king uses the Subjunctive/Imperfect to
express his threats and purpose concerning Yukhannan’s future.</em></p>
<p><strong>Sentence 1</strong></p>
<p>ܩܡ ܝܘܚܢܢ ܩܕܡ ܡܠܟܐ ܕܕܝܢܐ qām Yūḥannan qdām malkā d-dīnā. qām (stood)
Yūḥannan (John) qdām (before) malkā (the-king) d-dīnā (of-judgment). →
Yukhannan stood before the king of judgment.</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 2</strong></p>
<p>ܘܝܬܒ ܡܠܟܐ ܘܐܡܪ ܠܗ w-īteb malkā w-ʾemar l-ēh: w-īteb (and-sat) malkā
(the-king) w-ʾemar (and-said) l-ēh (to-him): → And the king sat and said
to him:</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 3</strong></p>
<p>ܥܒܕ ܐܢܐ ܕܝܢܐ ܕܐܥܒܕ ܒܝܫܐ ܠܟ ʿābed-nā dīnā, d-ʾeʿbed bīšā lāḵ! ʿābed
(doing/making) -nā (am-I) dīnā (judgment), d- (PURP) + ʾeʿbed
(1sg.IMPF.PEAL of ʿ-b-d, ‘do/make’ = “in order that I might do”) bīšā
(evil) lāḵ (to-you)! → “I am rendering judgment, that I might do evil to
you!” <em>Note: ʾeʿbed is a Peal imperfect 1sg in a purpose clause
(introduced by d-), not a perfect or imperative. The construction d- +
Imperfect corresponds to Greek ἵνα + subjunctive.</em></p>
<p><strong>Sentence 4</strong></p>
<p>ܐܢ ܠܐ ܬܫܒܘܩ ܐܪܥܝ ܢܩܛܠܘܢ ܠܟ ܒܝܘܡ ܕܝܢܐ ʾen lā tešbūq ʾarʿ-y, neqṭlūn
lāḵ b-yūm dīnā! ʾen (if) lā (not) tešbūq (you-will-leave) ʾarʿ-y
(land-my), neqṭlūn (they-will-kill) lāḵ (to-you) b-yūm (in-the-day) dīnā
(of-judgment)! → “If you do not leave my land, they will kill you in the
day of judgment!”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 5</strong></p>
<p>ܝܘܚܢܢ ܐܡܪ ܠܗ ܠܐ ܐܕܚܠ Yūḥannan ʾemar l-ēh: lā ʾedḥal. Yūḥannan (John)
ʾemar (said) l-ēh (to-him): lā (not) ʾedḥal (I-will-fear). → Yukhannan
said to him: “I will not fear.”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 6</strong></p>
<p>ܐܬܝܬ ܕܐܡܪ ܡܠܬܐ ܕܐܠܗܐ ܠܥܠܡܐ ʾetēt d-ʾemar meltā d-Alāhā l-ʿālmā. ʾetēt
(I-came) d-ʾemar (that-I-might-say) meltā (the-word) d-Alāhā (of-God)
l-ʿālmā (to-the-world). → “I came in order to speak the word of God to
the world.”</p>
<hr />

]]></text></questiontext></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 8</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[In the story, what does the king threaten to do to Yukhannan?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Have him killed in the day of judgment]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct (sentence 4).]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Throw him into prison]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in this part.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Send him back to the wilderness]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Banish him from the temple]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That was the chief priest in Lesson 6.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 9</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[What condition does the king set?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[If Yukhannan does not leave his land]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct: <i>ʾen lā tešbūq ʾarʿ-y</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[If Yukhannan does not stop preaching]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The condition is about leaving the land.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[If Yukhannan does not worship him]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[If Yukhannan does not pay tribute]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 10</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[What is Yukhannan's stated purpose for coming?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[To speak the word of God to the world]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct (sentence 6).]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[To become king]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[To judge the king]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[To leave the land]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[He says he will not fear.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 11</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[In sentence 3, what is <i>ʾeʿbed</i>?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Peal imperfect 1 c.sg. of ʿ-b-d in a purpose clause: 'that I might do']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Peal perfect 1 c.sg.: 'I did']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The ʾe- prefix marks the imperfect.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperative: 'do!']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[It follows <i>d-</i>: a purpose clause.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Participle: 'doing']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The participle is <i>ʿābed</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 12</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 1. Identify ܬܫܒܩܘܢ (<i>tešbqūn</i>).]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 2 m.pl.: 'you (pl.) will leave']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct: t- prefix with -ūn.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 3 m.pl.: 'they will leave']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[3 m.pl. takes n- (<i>nešbqūn</i>).]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 2 m.sg.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[-ūn marks the plural.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Perfect 2 m.pl.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The perfect has no prefix.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 13</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 1. Identify ܢܥܒܕܢ (<i>neʿbdān</i>).]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 3 f.pl.: 'they (f.) will do']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 3 m.pl.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That ends in -ūn.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 1 c.pl.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[1 c.pl. has no ending: <i>neʿbed</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Perfect 1 c.pl.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The n- is a prefix.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 14</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 1. Identify ܐܚܙܐ (<i>ʾeḥzē</i>, root ḥ-z-y).]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 1 c.sg.: 'I will see']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Perfect 3 m.sg.: 'he saw']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That is <i>ḥzā</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Aphel perfect: 'he showed']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[ʾe- here is the imperfect prefix.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Imperfect 3 m.sg.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[3 m.sg. takes n-: <i>neḥzē</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 15</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 2. Which forms are the Peal imperfect of q-ṭ-l for 'he will kill, we will kill, I will kill, they (m.) will kill'?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>neqṭūl, neqṭūl, ʾeqṭūl, neqṭlūn</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct: 3 m.sg. and 1 c.pl. look the same.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>teqṭūl, neqṭūl, ʾeqṭūl, teqṭlūn</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[t- marks the 2nd person (and 3 f.sg.).]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>neqṭūl, neqṭlūn, ʾeqṭūl, neqṭūl</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[-ūn is the plural ending for 'they'.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>qṭal, qṭaln, qeṭlet, qṭalū</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Those are perfect forms.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 16</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 3. Translate: <i>Npaq malkā d-neḥzē l-Yūḥannan.</i>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The king went out in order to see Yukhannan.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct: <i>d-</i> + imperfect = purpose.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The king went out and saw Yukhannan.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>d-neḥzē</i> is purpose, not a past fact.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Yukhannan went out to see the king.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>malkā</i> is the subject.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The king will go out and see Yukhannan.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>npaq</i> is perfect.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 17</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 3. Translate: <i>Lā neqṭūl malkā l-gabrā ṭābā.</i>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The king will not kill the good man.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The king did not kill the good man.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>neqṭūl</i> is imperfect.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[We will not kill the good king.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>malkā</i> is the subject.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The good man will not kill the king.]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>l-</i> marks the object.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
