<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Check 19</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 4. Which is the best Syriac for 'They (m.pl.) will come to the kingdom'?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>Nēthūn l-malkūttā.</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>ʾEtaw l-malkūttā.</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That is the perfect, 'they came'.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>Tēthūn l-malkūttā.</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[t- makes it 'you (pl.)'.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>Nētē l-malkūttā.</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That is 'he will come'.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="description"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 8 · Section 10: Grammatical Summary</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<h3>Section 10: Grammatical Summary</h3>
<p><strong>THE PEAL IMPERFECT (Root q-ṭ-l)</strong></p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style="text-align: left;">Person</th>
<th style="text-align: left;">Syriac</th>
<th style="text-align: left;">Translit</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;"><strong>3 m.sg.</strong></td>
<td style="text-align: left;">ܢܩܛܘܠ</td>
<td style="text-align: left;">neqṭūl (he will kill)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;"><strong>3 f.sg.</strong></td>
<td style="text-align: left;">ܬܩܛܘܠ</td>
<td style="text-align: left;">teqṭūl (she will kill)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;"><strong>2 m.sg.</strong></td>
<td style="text-align: left;">ܬܩܛܘܠ</td>
<td style="text-align: left;">teqṭūl (you will kill)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;"><strong>1 c.sg.</strong></td>
<td style="text-align: left;">ܐܩܛܘܠ</td>
<td style="text-align: left;">ʾeqṭūl (I will kill)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;"><strong>3 m.pl.</strong></td>
<td style="text-align: left;">ܢܩܛܠܘܢ</td>
<td style="text-align: left;">neqṭlūn (they will k.)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;"><strong>1 c.pl.</strong></td>
<td style="text-align: left;">ܢܩܛܘܠ</td>
<td style="text-align: left;">neqṭūl (we will kill)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>SYNTAX OF PURPOSE</strong></p>
<p>Verb 1 (Any Tense) + <code>d-</code> + Verb 2 (Imperfect) = Purpose
Clause <em>ʾEzal (He went) d-neʿbed (in order to do) qyāmā (a
covenant).</em></p>

